543 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Strengths of Ultrasonic Sensors: 1. Non-contact Measurement: Ultrasonic sensors measure distance without physical contact, making them suitable for various applications where contact sensors are not feasible. 2. High Accuracy: They offer high accuracy in distance measurement, making them suitable for precision applications. 3. Wide Range: Ultrasonic sensors can detect objects over a wide range, from a few centimeters to several meters, depending on the sensor's specifications. 4. Versatility: They can be used in diverse environments and conditions, including indoor and outdoor settings. 5. Immunity to Color and Transparency: Ultrasonic sensors can detect objects regardless of their color or transparency, unlike optical sensors. 6. Reliability: They are generally robust and reliable, with minimal susceptibility to environmental factors such as dust, light, or humidity. Weaknesses of Ultrasonic Sensors: 1. Limited Resolution: Ultrasonic sensors may have limited resolution compared to some other distance measurement technologies. 2. Sensitivity to Temperature Changes: Extreme temperature variations can affect the speed of sound in air, potentially impacting the accuracy of ultrasonic measurements.)
/E (Strengths of Ultrasonic Sensors: 1. Non-contact Measurement: Ultrasonic sensors measure distance without physical contact, making them suitable for various applications where contact sensors are not feasible. 2. High Accuracy: They offer high accuracy in distance measurement, making them suitable for precision applications. 3. Wide Range: Ultrasonic sensors can detect objects over a wide range, from a few centimeters to several meters, depending on the sensor's specifications. 4. Versatility: They can be used in diverse environments and conditions, including indoor and outdoor settings. 5. Immunity to Color and Transparency: Ultrasonic sensors can detect objects regardless of their color or transparency, unlike optical sensors. 6. Reliability: They are generally robust and reliable, with minimal susceptibility to environmental factors such as dust, light, or humidity. Weaknesses of Ultrasonic Sensors: 1. Limited Resolution: Ultrasonic sensors may have limited resolution compared to some other distance measurement technologies. 2. Sensitivity to Temperature Changes: Extreme temperature variations can affect the speed of sound in air, potentially impacting the accuracy of ultrasonic measurements.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
