547 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (  3. Beam Spread: Ultrasonic waves spread out as they travel, leading to a wider detection area and potential interference from nearby objects. 4. Reflective Surfaces: Highly reflective surfaces can cause echoes, leading to inaccuracies or false readings in distance measurement. 5. Limited Detection Range in Certain Conditions: Ultrasonic sensors may struggle to detect objects in conditions with heavy fog, rain, or dust, which can absorb or scatter ultrasonic waves. 6. Interference from Acoustic Noise: Background noise, such as loud machinery or other ultrasonic sensors nearby, can interfere with the sensor's operation, affecting accuracy.)
/E (  3. Beam Spread: Ultrasonic waves spread out as they travel, leading to a wider detection area and potential interference from nearby objects. 4. Reflective Surfaces: Highly reflective surfaces can cause echoes, leading to inaccuracies or false readings in distance measurement. 5. Limited Detection Range in Certain Conditions: Ultrasonic sensors may struggle to detect objects in conditions with heavy fog, rain, or dust, which can absorb or scatter ultrasonic waves. 6. Interference from Acoustic Noise: Background noise, such as loud machinery or other ultrasonic sensors nearby, can interfere with the sensor's operation, affecting accuracy.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
