/ActualText (ESP8266WiFi.h: This library provides support for the ESP8266 WiFi module, enabling it to connect to a Wi-Fi network and communicate over the internet. It includes functions for configuring and managing Wi-Fi connections, as well as sending and receiving data over Wi-Fi. This library is commonly utilized in IoT \(Internet of Things\) projects involving the ESP8266 module. In scenarios like the one presented here, where the Arduino board is equipped with an ESP8266 chip for wireless communication capabilities, ESP8266WiFi.h facilitates seamless integration with Wi-Fi networks, enabling remote communication and control.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
580 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1129 0 R
/ActualText (Servo.h: Servo.h is a library that facilitates the control of servo motors. Servo motors are frequently employed in projects requiring precise control of angular position, such as robotic arms, motorized doors, or in the case presented here, a parking barrier. This library simplifies servo motor control by offering functions to attach a servo motor to a specific pin, set its position, and detach it when not in use. In this code, Servo.h is employed to regulate the position of the parking barrier by adjusting the angle of the servo motor.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
581 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1130 0 R
/ActualText (LiquidCrystal.h: LiquidCrystal.h is a library used for controlling LCD \(Liquid Crystal Display\) modules, particularly those based on the Hitachi HD44780 controller or compatible controllers. This library simplifies the process of interfacing with and controlling LCD displays in Arduino projects. It provides functions for initializing the LCD, displaying text, moving the cursor, and other display-related operations. By including LiquidCrystal.h in your Arduino code, you can easily incorporate LCD displays into your projects and enhance user interfaces with visual feedback.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
